<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff; --fg: #1a1d21; --muted: #5c6470; --line: #dfe3e8;
    --panel: #f7f8fa; --accent: #2b5c8a; --warn: #8a5a00; --warn-bg: #fff6e0;
    --bad: #9b2226; --bad-bg: #fdeced; --ok: #1f6f43; --ok-bg: #e8f5ee;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #14171a; --fg: #e6e9ed; --muted: #9aa4b0; --line: #2b3138;
      --panel: #1c2025; --accent: #7fb2e0; --warn: #e5b567; --warn-bg: #33290f;
      --bad: #e88a8d; --bad-bg: #3a1d1f; --ok: #7dcfa0; --ok-bg: #16301f;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg);
    font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 62rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2.75rem 0 .75rem; padding-bottom: .4rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);
  }
  h3 { font-size: .95rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 .5rem; color: var(--muted);
       text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: .5rem 0 1rem; font-size: .875rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .45rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem;
       text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .panel { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line);
           border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.15rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .kv { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(11rem, auto) 1fr; gap: .3rem 1.25rem; }
  .kv dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  .kv dd { margin: 0; font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace; font-size: .82rem;
           word-break: break-all; }
  .badge { display: inline-block; padding: .1rem .5rem; border-radius: 999px;
           font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .badge.ok { background: var(--ok-bg); color: var(--ok); }
  .badge.warn { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn); }
  .badge.bad { background: var(--bad-bg); color: var(--bad); }
  .callout { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: .6rem .9rem;
             background: var(--panel); margin: .75rem 0; font-size: .9rem; }
  .callout.warn { border-left-color: var(--warn); background: var(--warn-bg); }
  .callout.bad { border-left-color: var(--bad); background: var(--bad-bg); }
  .funnel-bar { height: 1.35rem; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 3px; min-width: 2px; }
  pre { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px;
        padding: .9rem; overflow-x: auto; font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  ul.tight { margin: .4rem 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  ul.tight li { margin: .25rem 0; }
  .lim { margin: .9rem 0; }
  .lim strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .15rem; }
  .lim p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
           color: var(--muted); font-size: .82rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <p class="sub">
    morphline {{ provenance.pipeline_version }} &middot;
    {{ provenance.dataset }} ({{ provenance.dataset_version }}) &middot;
    {{ provenance.run_timestamp }}
  </p>

  {# ---- 1. Provenance (§2.8): a reader holding only this file must be able
         to reconstruct the run. ---- #}
  <h2>1. Provenance</h2>
  <div class="panel">
    <dl class="kv">
      <dt>pipeline_version</dt><dd>{{ provenance.pipeline_version }}</dd>
      <dt>git_sha</dt>
      <dd>
        {{ provenance.git_sha or "unavailable" }}
        {% if provenance.git_dirty %}<span class="badge bad">dirty</span>{% endif %}
      </dd>
      <dt>container_image</dt><dd>{{ provenance.container_image or "not containerised" }}</dd>
      <dt>container_digest</dt><dd>{{ provenance.container_digest or "n/a" }}</dd>
      <dt>python_version</dt><dd>{{ provenance.python_version }}</dd>
      <dt>platform</dt><dd>{{ provenance.platform }}</dd>
      <dt>nextflow_version</dt><dd>{{ provenance.nextflow_version or "not run under Nextflow" }}</dd>
      <dt>parser_version</dt><dd>{{ provenance.parser_version }}</dd>
      <dt>freesurfer_version(s)</dt>
      <dd>{{ provenance.freesurfer_versions | join(", ") or "none observed" }}</dd>
      <dt>dataset</dt><dd>{{ provenance.dataset }} / {{ provenance.dataset_version }}</dd>
      <dt>input_path</dt><dd>{{ provenance.input_path or "generated fixtures" }}</dd>
      <dt>random_seed(s)</dt>
      <dd>
        {% for k, v in provenance.random_seeds.items() %}{{ k }}={{ v }} {% endfor %}
        {% if not provenance.random_seeds %}none{% endif %}
      </dd>
      <dt>duration_seconds</dt>
      <dd>{{ "%.2f"|format(provenance.duration_seconds) if provenance.duration_seconds else "n/a" }}</dd>
    </dl>
    <h3>Fully resolved configuration</h3>
    <pre>{{ resolved_config }}</pre>
  </div>

  {# ---- 2. Data accounting funnel (§1.6): every drop needs a stated cause. ---- #}
  <h2>2. Data accounting funnel</h2>

  {% if reconciliation_errors %}
  <div class="callout bad">
    <strong>Funnel does not reconcile.</strong> Unexplained loss is a bug, not a
    rounding error.
    <ul class="tight">
      {% for err in reconciliation_errors %}<li>{{ err }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <div class="callout">
    <span class="badge ok">reconciles exactly</span>
    Every drop below has a stated cause.
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% set max_count = funnel | map(attribute='count') | max %}
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Boundary</th><th>Unit</th><th class="num">Count</th>
        <th class="num">Lost</th><th>Causes</th><th style="width:22%">&nbsp;</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in funnel %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.boundary }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.unit }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.count }}</td>
        <td class="num">
          {% if row.lost %}<span class="badge warn">{{ row.lost }}</span>{% else %}0{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>{{ row.causes or "—" }}</td>
        <td>
          <div class="funnel-bar"
               style="width: {{ (100 * row.count / max_count) if max_count else 0 }}%"></div>
        </td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  {% if parse_failures %}
  <h3>Parse failures by reason code</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Reason code</th><th class="num">Files</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for code, n in parse_failures.items() %}
      <tr><td>{{ code }}</td><td class="num">{{ n }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if missingness %}
  <h3>Missingness by cause</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Cause</th><th class="num">Sessions</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for cause, n in missingness.items() %}
      <tr><td>{{ cause }}</td><td class="num">{{ n }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  <h3>Metadata coverage</h3>
  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Distribution</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for field, counts in metadata_coverage.items() %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ field }}</td>
        <td>
          {% for k, v in counts.items() %}{{ k }}: {{ v }}{% if not loop.last %} &middot; {% endif %}{% endfor %}
          {% if not counts %}—{% endif %}
        </td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  {% if batch_sizes %}
  <h3>Batch sizes</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Site</th><th class="num">Subjects</th><th class="num">Observations</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for site, n in batch_sizes.get('subjects_per_site', {}).items() %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ site }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ n }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ batch_sizes.get('observations_per_site', {}).get(site, 0) }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if accounting_notes %}
  <div class="callout warn">
    <ul class="tight">
      {% for note in accounting_notes %}<li>{{ note }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {# ---- 3. QC (§2.4) ---- #}
  <h2>3. Quality control</h2>
  <div class="callout warn">
    <strong>v0.1.0 stub.</strong> No QC checks are implemented, so every
    observation is marked PASS. The three-level status model, the flag
    structure, and the analysis-inclusion policy are already in place; week 3
    fills in the checks and the sensitivity/specificity validation.
  </div>
  {% if qc_summary and qc_summary.by_status %}
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th class="num">Observations</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for status, n in qc_summary.by_status.items() %}
      <tr><td>{{ status }}</td><td class="num">{{ n }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {# ---- 4. Harmonization (§2.3) ---- #}
  <h2>4. Harmonization diagnostics</h2>

  {% if confound %}
  <div class="callout {{ 'bad' if not confound.interpretable else '' }}">
    <strong>Scanner &times; time confounding: {{ confound.severity }}.</strong>
    {{ confound.message }}
  </div>
  <dl class="kv">
    <dt>site explains var(time)</dt><dd>{{ "%.3f"|format(confound.max_site_time_r2) }}</dd>
    <dt>site/time correlation</dt><dd>{{ "%.3f"|format(confound.correlation) }}</dd>
    <dt>longitudinal estimates</dt>
    <dd>
      {% if confound.interpretable %}
        <span class="badge ok">interpretable with stated caveats</span>
      {% else %}
        <span class="badge bad">NOT interpretable as biology</span>
      {% endif %}
    </dd>
  </dl>
  {% endif %}

  {% if confound_crosstab %}
  <h3>Site &times; time-from-baseline crosstab</h3>
  <div class="scroll">{{ confound_crosstab | safe }}</div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if small_batches %}
  <h3>Batches below min_batch_size</h3>
  <p class="sub">
    Reported, never silently dropped. The threshold is a conservative
    engineering default for stability, not a methodological law — adequacy
    depends on the number of batches, covariate balance within batch, outcome
    variance, and the magnitude of the batch effect relative to it.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Batch</th><th class="num">Subjects</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for batch, n in small_batches.items() %}
      <tr><td>{{ batch }}</td><td class="num">{{ n }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if harmonization_notes %}
  <div class="callout">
    <ul class="tight">
      {% for note in harmonization_notes %}<li>{{ note }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {# ---- 5. Model results (§2.5) ---- #}
  <h2>5. Model results</h2>
  <div class="callout warn">
    <strong>Sensitivity analysis, not validated biological inference.</strong>
    Harmonized and unharmonized estimates show how conclusions depend on the
    harmonization assumption; they do not establish which is correct.
  </div>

  <dl class="kv">
    <dt>specification</dt>
    <dd>value ~ age_baseline + time + dx_baseline + time:dx_baseline + sex + etiv_baseline</dd>
    <dt>random effects</dt><dd>intercept + slope on time, grouped by subject_id</dd>
    <dt>primary family size</dt><dd>{{ model.family_size }} test(s)</dd>
    <dt>FDR alpha</dt><dd>{{ model.fdr_alpha }}</dd>
    <dt>convergence rate</dt><dd>{{ "%.0f%%"|format(100 * model.convergence_rate) }}</dd>
    <dt>modeled observations</dt><dd>{{ model.n_modeled_observations }}</dd>
  </dl>

  <div class="scroll">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Region</th><th>Measure</th><th class="num">N obs</th><th class="num">N subj</th>
        <th>Converged</th><th class="num">Estimate</th><th class="num">SE</th>
        <th class="num">p</th><th class="num">q</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in model_rows %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.region }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.measure_type }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.n_observations }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.n_subjects }}</td>
        <td>
          {% if row.converged %}<span class="badge ok">yes</span>
          {% else %}<span class="badge bad">no</span>{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.4f"|format(row.estimate) if row.estimate is not none else "—" }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.4f"|format(row.std_error) if row.std_error is not none else "—" }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.4g"|format(row.p_value) if row.p_value is not none else "—" }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.4g"|format(row.q_value) if row.q_value is not none else "—" }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p class="sub">
    Estimate and p-value are for the <code>time &times; diagnosis</code>
    interaction — the primary hypothesis. Hemispheres are independent tests and
    are counted in the multiplicity family.
  </p>

  {% if model.notes %}
  <div class="callout">
    <ul class="tight">
      {% for note in model.notes %}<li>{{ note }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {# ---- 6. Limitations ----
     Standing limitations are presentation text and live here rather than in
     report.py, so that naming input-format specifics does not drag format
     vocabulary into a downstream stage module (§1.4). Run-dependent findings
     are supplied by the stage. ---- #}
  <h2>6. Limitations</h2>

  {% for item in dynamic_limitations %}
  <div class="lim">
    <strong>{{ item.title }}</strong>
    <p>{{ item.body }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

  <div class="lim">
    <strong>Walking skeleton, not a validated analysis</strong>
    <p>
      This is v0.1.0. QC marks every observation PASS, harmonization is an
      identity transform, and the model fits a single region. No number in
      this report should be read as a finding.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="lim">
    <strong>pybids is not a derivatives parser</strong>
    <p>
      pybids indexes raw BIDS well, but its BIDS-Derivatives support is
      partial, and FreeSurfer's native subject-directory output is not
      BIDS-organized at all. morphline uses a purpose-built resolver for
      FreeSurfer conventions and reserves pybids for raw layout traversal
      inside adapters.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="lim">
    <strong>Harmonized results are sensitivity analysis, not inference</strong>
    <p>
      Running harmonized and unharmonized models shows how conclusions depend
      on the harmonization assumption. It does not establish which is correct.
      Where scanner is confounded with time, the biological longitudinal
      effect and the scanner effect are not identifiable from the observed
      data alone — a property of the study design, not a deficiency in the
      software.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="lim">
    <strong>Missingness is assumed missing-at-random</strong>
    <p>
      Mixed-effects models use all available observations and handle
      unbalanced longitudinal designs naturally, but validity rests on a MAR
      assumption. That assumption is questionable in aging cohorts, where
      dropout can be caused by the disease progression under study, and where
      QC failure is plausibly associated with atrophy severity and motion.
      v1 does not attempt MNAR modeling — no pattern-mixture models, selection
      models, or joint dropout modeling.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="lim">
    <strong>Synthetic data only</strong>
    <p>
      These results come from synthetic fixtures with injected ground truth.
      That validates <em>statistical recovery</em> — whether the methods
      recover known truth — and cannot validate that the parser handles real
      headers and real metadata. Those are different questions, and both are
      needed. Real-data integration is a later milestone.
    </p>
  </div>

  <footer>
    Generated by morphline {{ provenance.pipeline_version }}. This report is
    self-contained: it fetches no external assets and can be archived or read
    offline.
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
